+## Optional constructive repair — 2026-10-24
+
+The issued v2.1.0 source had reproduced contract defects: no `RULE_HASH`, unknown
+controls were accepted, several advertised texture/palette axes were dead or
+contradictory, and its component-count/domain declarations disagreed with its
+validator. It has been replaced by a proposed v3.0.0 constructive sampler at
+SHA-256 `9f6636375ff2d31e75cac70dbe840a6030e665d91f73c59fccda1fcdee4e5472`,
+pinned to canonical rule hash `f9d83b4de683`.
+
+The repaired sampler exposes only exact observable controls (`grid_h` 7..9,
+`grid_w` 9..11, `n` 2..4), rejects malformed calls, and uses finite candidate
+banks plus backtracking rather than retry/fallback placement. Every ordinary
+scene contains a border component extending inward and an interior component one
+cell from a border. The four-slot count/side schedule teaches whole-component
+recoloring, exact border contact, preservation, side coverage, and varying
+border-component counts.
+
+Verification on the final source: 30 portable tests passed; lint, override, and
+semantic gates passed; a reusable `workspace/adversarial_review.py` executed 24
+cases through protected canonical Racket with zero label mismatches. All six
+declared rivals were refuted (three on 24/24 cases and three on 12/24). One
+broader inherited `rule_smoke` invocation was interrupted before a verdict and
+is not represented as passing. This optional repair remains owner-integration
+and approval pending.
